{"name":"Queen Palm","hex":"#ad9e4b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"queen palm","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Syagrus romanzoffiana, a medium-sized palm native to South America, widely planted in the tropics and subtropics for the fine texture of its fronds"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/queen_palm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Syagrus romanzoffiana","blocks":[{"text":"Syagrus romanzoffiana, the queen palm, cocos palm or Jerivá, is a palm native to South America, introduced throughout the world as a popular ornamental garden tree. S. romanzoffiana is a medium-sized palm, quickly reaching maturity at a height of up to 15 m (49 ft) tall, with pinnate leaves having as many as 494 pinnae (leaflets), although more typically around 300, each pinna being around 50 centimetres (18 in) in length and 3–5 centimetres (1–2 in) in width."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Jeriv%C3%A1_%28do_tupi_iara%27yb%C3%A1%29_com_frutos_ainda_verdes_06.jpg/330px-Jeriv%C3%A1_%28do_tupi_iara%27yb%C3%A1%29_com_frutos_ainda_verdes_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syagrus_romanzoffiana"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Frutos_do_jeriv%C3%A1_%28do_tupi_iara%27yb%C3%A1%29_-_54964354091.jpg/500px-Frutos_do_jeriv%C3%A1_%28do_tupi_iara%27yb%C3%A1%29_-_54964354091.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Frutos_do_jeriv%C3%A1_%28do_tupi_iara%27yb%C3%A1%29_-_54964354091.jpg/1280px-Frutos_do_jeriv%C3%A1_%28do_tupi_iara%27yb%C3%A1%29_-_54964354091.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Frutos_do_jeriv%C3%A1_%28do_tupi_iara%27yb%C3%A1%29_-_54964354091.jpg/500px-Frutos_do_jeriv%C3%A1_%28do_tupi_iara%27